# Riverwalk Technique, the first mode: "The owner of target nonland permanent puts it on their choice of the top or bottom of their
# library." Bot2 has an Island and an Ornithopter: the Island is not a legal target (the refusal). Bot1 targets the Ornithopter and its
# owner Bot2 puts it on top (Accept), so it draws it again in turn 4.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Black Lotus
Riverwalk Technique
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Riverwalk Technique.Cast
Bot1.Modes(The owner of target nonland permanent)
! Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Island)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Accept
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter = (absent)
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot2.Hand.Count = 7
? Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Colors.Count = 0

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Riverwalk Technique; Black Lotus
